Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:16:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add oracle interface EvmTxRead (8)

One finalized EVM transaction: block number, block hash, block timestamp,
position, sender, recipient, native value, nonce, type, status and log
count. The sibling of EvmLogRead: EvmLogRead returns what a transaction
emitted, EvmTxRead returns when and by whom, so a contract can accept a
token transfer only if it was made after a given moment. A reverted
transaction is a final answer (status 0). getBlockDateAndTime converts
the block time to a QPI DateAndTime for comparison with qpi.now().
Same chains and fee as EvmLogRead. Registered in oracle_interfaces_def.h;
tests added to test/oracle_engine.cpp.
Reference service: oracle-machine oracles/read_evm_tx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHXGjDwxBARUytE2smA8oq
